{
 "id": "tr-a1-possessive-suffixes",
 "cefr": "A1",
 "title": "Possessive suffixes (İyelik ekleri)",
 "subtitle": "Marking ownership directly on the possessed noun",
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "what-is-it",
   "title": "what is it?",
   "body": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "A possessive suffix is a short ending attached to a noun to show who owns or is associated with it. Turkish has one suffix for each grammatical person: "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-(I)m"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (my), "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-(I)n"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (your, singular), "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-(s)I"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (his/her/its), "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-(I)mIz"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (our), "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-(I)nIz"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (your, plural/formal), and "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-lArI"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (their). The high vowel I in these suffixes obeys four-way vowel harmony and the A in -lArI two-way harmony (a/e), so the actual vowel used depends on the last vowel of the stem. The suffix is added to the "
      },
      {
       "kind": "strong",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "possessed noun"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": ", not to the possessor."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "when-to-use-it",
   "title": "when to use it",
   "body": [
    {
     "kind": "list",
     "items": [
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Expressing ownership or belonging."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " Use a possessive suffix whenever you want to say that something belongs to a person: "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "evim"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " (my house), "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "kitabın"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " (your book)."
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Referring to body parts and personal items."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " Turkish regularly uses possessive suffixes where English might omit the possessive: "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "gözüm"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " (my eye)."
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Possessive constructions with a named possessor."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " When the possessor is a noun or pronoun (not just implied), it takes the genitive suffix "
         },
         {
          "kind": "mono",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "-(n)In"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ", and the possessed noun still carries the possessive suffix: "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Ahmet'in arabası"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " (Ahmet's car)."
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "formation",
   "title": "formation",
   "body": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "The buffer vowel "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "(I)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " in the suffixes below stands for whichever of "
      },
      {
       "kind": "strong",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "ı, i, u, ü"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " matches the last vowel of the stem. It appears only when the stem ends in a "
      },
      {
       "kind": "strong",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "consonant"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": ". When the stem ends in a "
      },
      {
       "kind": "strong",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "vowel"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": ", the buffer vowel is dropped entirely for 1sg, 2sg, 1pl, and 2pl. For 3sg, a "
      },
      {
       "kind": "strong",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "buffer consonant -s-"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " is inserted instead (arabası). The 3pl suffix -lArI begins with a consonant, so it is the same after consonants and vowels (evleri, arabaları)."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "conjugation-table",
     "head": [
      "person",
      "suffix (after consonant)",
      "suffix (after vowel)",
      "example stem: ev (house)",
      "example stem: araba (car)"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "1sg (my)",
       "-(I)m",
       "-m",
       "evim",
       "arabam"
      ],
      [
       "2sg (your)",
       "-(I)n",
       "-n",
       "evin",
       "araban"
      ],
      [
       "3sg (his/her/its)",
       "-(s)I",
       "-sI",
       "evi",
       "arabası"
      ],
      [
       "1pl (our)",
       "-(I)mIz",
       "-mIz",
       "evimiz",
       "arabamız"
      ],
      [
       "2pl (your, pl.)",
       "-(I)nIz",
       "-nIz",
       "eviniz",
       "arabanız"
      ],
      [
       "3pl (their)",
       "-lArI",
       "-lArI",
       "evleri",
       "arabaları"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "callout",
     "variant": "default",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "paragraph",
       "text": [
        {
         "kind": "strong",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "Vowel harmony reminder."
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": " The "
        },
        {
         "kind": "mono",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "I"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": " in each suffix follows the last vowel of the stem: back-unrounded (a, ı) → "
        },
        {
         "kind": "mono",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "ı"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "; front-unrounded (e, i) → "
        },
        {
         "kind": "mono",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "i"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "; back-rounded (o, u) → "
        },
        {
         "kind": "mono",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "u"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "; front-rounded (ö, ü) → "
        },
        {
         "kind": "mono",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "ü"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": ". So "
        },
        {
         "kind": "em",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "göz"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": " (eye) → "
        },
        {
         "kind": "em",
         "children": [
          {
           "kind": "text",
           "text": "gözüm"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": " (my eye)."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-in-context",
   "title": "examples in context",
   "body": [
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "This is my house.",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Bu "
      },
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "evim"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "."
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Consonant-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "ev"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " + 1sg suffix "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-im"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (front-unrounded harmony)."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "Where is your book?",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "Kitabın"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " nerede?"
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Consonant-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "kitap"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " undergoes consonant mutation to "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "kitab-"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " before a vowel suffix, then 2sg "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-ın"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " is added."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "Ahmet's car is big.",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Ahmet'in "
      },
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "arabası"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " büyük."
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Vowel-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "araba"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " + 3sg suffix "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-sı"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (buffer consonant -s- required after a vowel)."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "Our house is small.",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "Evimiz"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " küçük."
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Consonant-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "ev"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " + 1pl suffix "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-imiz"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "My eye is dark.",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "Gözüm"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " siyah."
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Consonant-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "göz"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " + 1sg suffix "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-üm"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " (front-rounded harmony: ö/ü → ü)."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "example",
     "en": "My car is here.",
     "target": [
      {
       "kind": "hilite",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "Arabam"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " burada."
      }
     ],
     "note": [
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Vowel-final stem "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "araba"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " + 1sg suffix "
      },
      {
       "kind": "mono",
       "children": [
        {
         "kind": "text",
         "text": "-m"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "kind": "text",
       "text": " — no buffer vowel after a vowel-final stem."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "common-pitfalls",
   "title": "common pitfalls",
   "body": [
    {
     "kind": "list",
     "items": [
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Confusing 1sg -(I)m with 3sg -(s)I."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Evim"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " means «my house»; "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "evi"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " means «his/her house». The 3sg suffix on a consonant-final stem is just "
         },
         {
          "kind": "mono",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "-I"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " (no leading consonant), so it is shorter than the 1sg form. Keep the two distinct."
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Dropping the -s- buffer in 3sg after a vowel-final stem."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " The 3sg suffix after a vowel is "
         },
         {
          "kind": "mono",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "-sI"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ", not "
         },
         {
          "kind": "mono",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "-I"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ". Writing "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "*arabaı"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " is incorrect; the correct form is "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "arabası"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ". The buffer consonant -s- prevents two vowels from colliding."
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Putting the possessive suffix on the possessor instead of the possessed noun."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " In Turkish, the possessor takes the "
         },
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "genitive suffix"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " and the possessed noun takes the "
         },
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "possessive suffix"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ". "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Ahmet'in arabası"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " is correct (genitive on Ahmet, possessive on araba), not "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "*Ahmet'im araba"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "."
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": [
         {
          "kind": "strong",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Inserting a buffer vowel after a vowel-final stem."
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " The buffer vowel "
         },
         {
          "kind": "mono",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "(I)"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " only appears after consonant-final stems. After a vowel-final stem, it is dropped. "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "*Arabaım"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " and "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "*kapıım"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " are both wrong; the correct forms are "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "arabam"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " and "
         },
         {
          "kind": "em",
          "children": [
           {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "kapım"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "."
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}